 Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.
   The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
   Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

   Task 1: Disable swap
   Description Task 1: This task will disable swap if the variable vault_hardening_disable_swap is set to true. It will first turn off swap using the swapoff command, and then it will remove the swap entry from the fstab file using the mount module.

   Task 2: Disable core dumps
   Description Task 2: This task will disable core dumps if the variable vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps is set to true. It will loop through a set of limits and domain values and set them using the pam_limits module to prevent core dumps.

   Task 3: Disable Shell Command History
   Description Task 3: This task will disable shell command history if the variable vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history is set to true. It will copy a script that sets the HISTIGNORE environment variable to exclude vault commands into the /etc/profile.d/ directory.

   Task 4: Configure SELinux / AppArmor
   Description Task 4: This task will configure SELinux and AppArmor if the variable vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor is set to true. It will first check if SELinux is enabled and if so, it will install the selinux-policy package and set the SELinux policy to targeted and enforcing. It will then check if AppArmor is enabled and if so, it will enable the AppArmor profile for the vault binary.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Disable swap
  become: true
  block:
    - name: Turn off swap
      command: swapoff -a
      when: vault_hardening_disable_swap | bool

    - name: Remove swap entry from fstab
      mount:
        name: "{{ item.device }}"
        fstype: swap
        state: absent
      with_items: "{{ ansible_mounts }}"
      when: vault_hardening_disable_swap | bool and ansible_mounts is defined

- name: Disable core dumps
  become: true
  block:
    - name: Set limits to prevent core dumps
      pam_limits:
        domain: "{{ item.domain }}"
        limit_type: "{{ item.limit_type }}"
        limit_item: "{{ item.limit_item }}"
        value: "{{ item.value }}"
      loop:
        - { domain: "*", limit_type: "hard", limit_item: "core", value: 0 }
        - { domain: "*", limit_type: "soft", limit_item: "core", value: 0 }
      when: vault_hardening_disable_core_dumps | bool

- name: Disable Shell Command History
  become: true
  block:
    - name: Copy script to disable command history
      copy:
        dest: /etc/profile.d/disable_vault_history.sh
        content: |
          export HISTIGNORE='*vault*:exit:logout:clear'
        mode: '0755'
      when: vault_hardening_disable_shell_command_history | bool

- name: Configure SELinux / AppArmor
  become: true
  block:
    - name: Install SELinux policy package
      package:
        name: selinux-policy
        state: present
      when: vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor | bool and 
            ansible_selinux.status == "enabled"

    - name: Set SELinux policy to targeted and enforcing
      selinux:
        policy: targeted
        state: enforcing
      when: vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor | bool and 
            ansible_selinux.status == "enabled"

    - name: Enable AppArmor profile for vault
      command: aa-enforce /etc/apparmor.d/usr.bin.vault
      when: vault_hardening_configure_selinux_apparmor | bool and 
            ansible_apparmor.status == "enabled"


