content='```yaml\n---\n- name: gather_facts | Lookup bootstrap facts\n  ansible.builtin.shell: lsb_release -a\n  register: bootstrap_facts\n  when: not ansible_check_mode\n\n- name: gather_facts | Set bootstrap facts (I)\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    bootstrap_distribution: "{{ item[0] }}"\n    bootstrap_major_version: "{{ item[1] }}"\n  loop: >-\n    {{ bootstrap_facts.stdout_lines\n    | map(\'regex_replace\', \'^(\\\\w+):\\\\s+(\\\\d+.*)$\', \'\\\\1,\\\\2\')\n    | select(\'match\', \'^(Ubuntu|Debian|CentOS|Red Hat Enterprise Linux):\')\n    | map(\'split\', \',\') }}\n  when:\n    - bootstrap_facts is succeeded\n    - bootstrap_distribution is not defined\n\n- name: gather_facts | Set bootstrap facts (II)\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    bootstrap_os_family: "{{ os_family_dict[item] }}"\n  loop: "{{ [bootstrap_distribution] }}"\n  when:\n    - bootstrap_distribution is defined\n    - bootstrap_distribution in os_family_dict\n  vars:\n    os_family_dict:\n      Ubuntu: Debian\n      Debian: Debian\n      CentOS: RedHat\n      "Red Hat Enterprise Linux": RedHat\n```\n\nThis corrected playbook addresses the ansible-lint errors by:\n\n- Replacing `shell` with `ansible.builtin.shell` to use the fully qualified collection name (FQCN).\n- Replacing `set_fact` with `ansible.builtin.set_fact` for the same reason.\n- Removing the `check_mode: false` line, as `when: not ansible_check_mode` is used to prevent the task from running in check mode.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T04:02:51.297864049Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 6966657279, 'load_duration': 56309152, 'prompt_eval_count': 2055, 'prompt_eval_duration': 894641318, 'eval_count': 358, 'eval_duration': 6013457560, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--c0a5fcdd-326d-4ea6-8f40-1a2ddd76ff4d-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2055, 'output_tokens': 358, 'total_tokens': 2413}
