 Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.
   The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).
   Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.

Task 1: Assert usage of systemd as an init system
Description Task 1: This task verifies that the system's init system is systemd. If not, it will raise an error with the message "This module only works with systemd".

Task 2: Get the latest release version of Promtail from GitHub
Description Task 2: This task retrieves the latest release version of Promtail from GitHub's API. It uses the GitHub API credentials stored in the environment variables GH_USER and GH_TOKEN. If the release version is set to "latest", it fetches the latest version from GitHub. The task is delegated to localhost and runs once.

Task 3: Check if the local Promtail binary archive exists
Description Task 3: This task checks if the local Promtail binary archive exists in the directory specified by promtail_binary_local_dir. If the directory is specified, it asserts that the binary exists. If the binary does not exist, it raises an error with the message "When using 'promtail_binary_local_dir' please ensure that the binary exists". The task is delegated to localhost and runs once.

Task 4: Get the checksum for the Promtail binary
Description Task 4: This task retrieves the checksum for the Promtail binary. If promtail_binary_local_dir is not specified, it fetches the checksum list from GitHub's releases page and sets the checksum for the specified architecture (go_arch). The task runs once.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---
- name: Assert usage of systemd as an init system
  assert:
    that: ansible_facts.init_system == "systemd"
    fail_msg: "This module only works with systemd"
    success_msg: "Systemd is the init system"

- name: Get the latest release version of Promtail from GitHub
  uri:
    url: "https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/promtail/releases/latest"
    method: GET
    headers:
      Authorization: "token {{ lookup('env', 'GH_TOKEN') }}"
    delegate_to: localhost
  register: promtail_release
  until: promtail_release.status == 200
  retries: 5
  delay: 2
  run_once: true

- name: Check if the local Promtail binary archive exists
  stat:
    path: "{{ promtail_binary_local_dir }}/promtail"
  register: promtail_binary_stat
  delegate_to: localhost
  run_once: true

- name: Assert local Promtail binary exists
  assert:
    that: promtail_binary_stat.stat.exists
    fail_msg: "When using 'promtail_binary_local_dir' please ensure that the binary exists"
    success_msg: "Local Promtail binary exists"

- name: Get the checksum for the Promtail binary
  uri:
    url: "https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/promtail/releases/latest"
    method: GET
    headers:
      Authorization: "token {{ lookup('env', 'GH_TOKEN') }}"
    delegate_to: localhost
  register: promtail_release
  until: promtail_release.status == 200
  retries: 5
  delay: 2
  run_once: true

- name: Set checksum for the specified architecture
  set_fact:
    promtail_checksum: >-
      {{ promtail_release.json.assets | selectattr('name',
      'match', 'promtail_' ~ go_arch ~ '_linux.tar.gz.sha256') |
      map(attribute='browser_download_url') | list | first }}
  delegate_to: localhost
  run_once: true


