content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Restore etcd - get all nodes\n  hosts: localhost\n  gather_facts: no\n  tasks:\n    - name: Retrieve all node names in the RKE2 cluster\n      command: kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath=\'{.items[*].metadata.name}\'\n      register: all_node_names\n\n    - name: Store node names in variable\n      set_fact:\n        node_names: "{{ all_node_names.stdout_lines }}"\n\n- name: Restore etcd - remove old nodes\n  hosts: localhost\n  gather_facts: no\n  tasks:\n    - name: Remove nodes not in current inventory\n      command: kubectl delete node {{ item }}\n      loop: "{{ node_names | difference(groups[\'rke2_cluster_group_name\']) }}"\n      when: "\'{{ item }}\' not in groups[\'rke2_cluster_group_name\']"\n```\n\nThis playbook is structured to be included in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory. It uses two tasks to first retrieve all node names in the RKE2 cluster and then remove any nodes not present in the current inventory.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T05:13:36.739615479Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 5636571946, 'load_duration': 2449518483, 'prompt_eval_count': 370, 'prompt_eval_duration': 291412111, 'eval_count': 233, 'eval_duration': 2894443813, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--dc926cc6-a26b-426f-910c-d45af6bf5ca0-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 370, 'output_tokens': 233, 'total_tokens': 603}
